        "content": "{\"formal\": {\"statement\": \"open Set Function Filter Topology in\\n∀ (a b : ℕ → ℕ)\\n    (h' : Summable fun n ↦ (1 : ℝ) / a n)\\n    (h'' : ∀ n, b n = {k | a k ≤ n}.ncard), Tendsto (fun n ↦ (b n : ℝ) / n) atTop (𝓝 0)\", \"namespace\": \"\", \"supporting_declarations\": [], \"rendered\": \"∀ (a b : (ℕ → ℕ)),\\n  ((Summable fun n => (1 / ↑(a n))) →\\n    ((∀ (n : ℕ), ((b n) = {k | ((a k) ≤ n)}.ncard)) → (Filter.Tendsto (fun n => (↑(b n) / ↑n)) Filter.atTop (𝓝 0))))\"}, \"signature\": \"(a b : ℕ → ℕ)\\n    (h' : Summable fun n ↦ (1 : ℝ) / a n)\\n    (h'' : ∀ n, b n = {k | a k ≤ n}.ncard) :\\n    Tendsto (fun n ↦ (b n : ℝ) / n) atTop (𝓝 0)\", \"informal\": \"Let $a_n$ be a sequence of positive integers such that $\\\\sum_{n=1}^{\\\\infty} 1/a_n$ converges. For all $n$, let $b_n$ be the number of $a_n$ which are at most $n$. Prove that $\\\\lim_{n \\\\to \\\\infty} b_n/n = 0$.\", \"docstring\": \"/--\\nLet $a_n$ be a sequence of positive integers such that $\\\\sum_{n=1}^{\\\\infty} 1/a_n$ converges. For all $n$, let $b_n$ be the number of $a_n$ which are at most $n$. Prove that $\\\\lim_{n \\\\to \\\\infty} b_n/n = 0$.\\n-/\", \"prechecks\": {\"status\": \"completed\", \"hints\": [{\"kind\": \"natural_arithmetic_review\", \"status\": \"advisory\"}, {\"kind\": \"division_review\", \"status\": \"advisory\"}], \"vacuity\": \"unresolved\"}, \"advisory\": {\"paraphrase_status\": \"completed\", \"differences\": [\"The model uses 'functions' instead of 'sequence of positive integers'.\"], \"paraphrase\": \"For all functions a and b from natural numbers to natural numbers, if the series of 1/a_n converges, then the limit of b_n/n as n approaches infinity is 0, where b_n is the number of a_k's less than or equal to n.\", \"comparison_status\": \"completed\"}}"
